# File Organization

This rule is the file-organization source of truth for this repo. It supersedes the hybrid `sections/` pattern from the cross-project React style guide.

**Core model — colocate, then lift to the nearest common ancestor:**

1. **Route.** A component/hook/util/type used by only one `page.tsx` lives inside that route's own folder.
2. **Feature.** Reused by a sibling route within the same top-level feature (e.g. shared between `works/[slug]` and `works/new`) → lifts one level to that feature's own folder, e.g. `app/works/_components/`.
3. **Route group.** Reused across different features but still within one route group (e.g. both under `(site)`) → lifts to the route-group root, e.g. `app/(site)/_components/`.
4. **Root.** Only for components consumed by root layout or reused on multiple pages across the site → `components/`, `hooks/`, `lib/`, `types/` (this repo has no `src/` prefix).

The same lift logic applies uniformly to components and to non-component logic (hooks/lib/types) — one mental model, not two. Root `components/` is expected to stay small (mostly `ui/` shadcn primitives). Feature chrome that is only used inside a route group stays under that group's `_components/`.

**Folder naming:** non-route folders at every level are underscore-prefixed — `_components/`, `_hooks/`, `_lib/`, `_types/` (mirrors root's category names; there is no generic catch-all `utils/`). This applies one level deep inside an individual component's own folder too (e.g. `hero-section/_components/`, `hero-section/_hooks/`). Root-level folders keep bare names (`components/`, `hooks/`, `lib/`, `types/`). Server-only code that is not route-scoped lives under `server/`.

**Component shape:** defaults to a single kebab-case file (`user-menu.tsx`). Once it needs child components, a component-local hook, and/or its own async Suspense boundary, it becomes a folder of the same kebab-case name:

- `index.tsx` — the component itself
- `_components/` — children
- `_hooks/` — local hooks
- `skeleton.tsx` / `error.tsx` — loading and error fallback UI as direct siblings of `index.tsx`

Kebab-case applies whether it's a file or a folder — no rename when a component graduates from one to the other.

## Skeletons

- Every component folder that suspends or awaits data may have a sibling `skeleton.tsx`.
- Child components can own their own `skeleton.tsx`. Parents compose child skeletons instead of one mega-skeleton — easier to maintain when a child layout changes.
- Skeleton only data-dependent leaves (cards, images, API text). Keep structural headings/nav as real content when they don't depend on async data.
- Match the loaded layout (no reflow); prefer `animate-pulse` for placeholders.

## Hygiene

- Promote on second use — leave route-local until a sibling needs it
- No vanity barrels; import the file directly
- shadcn primitives stay one-per-file in `components/ui/`
